        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): add SIGKILL escalation after SIGTERM for stale MCP child cleanup",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`killStaleComputerUseMcpChildren` in `extensions/codex/src/app-server/computer-use.ts:1146` sends `process.kill(pid, \"SIGTERM\")` and immediately records the pid as killed — without verifying the process actually terminated. If a child process traps or ignores SIGTERM (e.g. `process.on('SIGTERM', ...)` without `process.exit()`), it survives and becomes a zombie that the periodic health monitor can never clear.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe fix schedules a SIGKILL after a 2-second grace period, matching the existing SIGTERM → SIGKILL escalation pattern already used in `node-cli-sessions.ts:293-294`. Before sending SIGKILL, it **revalidates process identity**: re-lists processes via `/bin/ps`, finds the PID, and confirms the command still matches a scoped `SkyComputerUseClient` MCP child descendant of the original ancestor PID. This prevents accidental termination of an unrelated process in the rare case of PID reuse during the grace period.\n\nThe timer is `unref()`'d so it does not keep the event loop alive.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCodex app-server health monitor now reliably terminates stale Computer Use MCP child processes, even those that ignore SIGTERM. PID reuse is guarded by identity revalidation before escalation.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Vitest (36/36 passed)\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/codex/src/app-server/computer-use.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  36 passed (36)\n```\n\nNew tests cover:\n- SIGTERM is sent to identified stale MCP children\n- After 2s grace period, revalidation ps confirms identity → SIGKILL is sent\n- After 2s, quick existence check (`kill 0`) throws ESRCH → SIGKILL skipped (process already exited)\n- After 2s, revalidation ps shows different command → SIGKILL skipped (PID reused by unrelated process)\n\n### Mutation check\n\nRevert the SIGKILL escalation → `revalidates process identity and sends SIGKILL` fails:\n\n```\n FAIL  killStaleComputerUseMcpChildren > revalidates process identity and sends SIGKILL\nAssertionError: expected \"kill\" to be called with arguments: [ 1234, 'SIGKILL' ]\nReceived: 1st call: [ 1234, 'SIGTERM' ]  // no SIGKILL call after timer\n```\n\nRestore fix → 36/36 passed.\n\n### Format check\n\n```\n$ oxfmt --check extensions/codex/src/app-server/computer-use.ts extensions/codex/src/app-server/computer-use.test.ts\nAll matched files use the correct format.\n```\n\n### Not tested\n\n- Live macOS `ps` process listing and process tree traversal (function gated to `darwin`; `parsePsOutput` and `isDescendantOfPid` production helpers are exercised through the mock data)\n- Real SIGTERM-ignoring child processes on macOS\n\n🤖 Generated with [co-mind](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
